# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# MS Office lock files (created when an .xlsx / .docx is open in Office;
# should never be committed — they are per-session, per-user, ephemeral).
~$*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Test artefacts
test-results/
playwright-report/
.lighthouseci/

# Local config
.env
.env.local

# Local Claude config (gitignored — per-machine secrets/preferences)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Local-only, NOT part of the website (added 2026-06-19 when the standalone JLPT/ workbook folder
# was consolidated into this repo): the N4 print-workbook build pipeline + an archive of
# superseded/backup files. Kept on disk but never committed to the website repo.
#
# EXCEPTION added 2026-09-30: the practice-bank validator and its inputs ARE committed, ~205 KB,
# so CI can run them (see .github/workflows/content-integrity.yml, job n4-integrity). On
# 2026-09-29 a data/ change flipped 24 glyphs out of the n5_prerequisite set and broke scope
# validation on 5 items while all 43 repo invariants stayed green - practice_validate.py is the
# only gate that reads that set, and being ignored meant CI could not see it. `_refcache/` stays
# out: the script falls back to the bundled 11 KB _jmdict_index.json, which was verified to reach
# the same verdict on all 15 banks and to still catch a planted non-word.
#
# Re-including a file inside an ignored directory needs the parent directories re-included first,
# hence the walk rather than a bare `/N4/Workbook/`.
/N4/Workbook/*
!/N4/Workbook/N4_Kanji_Workbook/
/N4/Workbook/N4_Kanji_Workbook/*
!/N4/Workbook/N4_Kanji_Workbook/practice_validate.py
!/N4/Workbook/N4_Kanji_Workbook/_jmdict_index.json
!/N4/Workbook/N4_Kanji_Workbook/*_bank.json
/Not required/

# Local prototype/working folder, not website content (added 2026-09-30). Holds the user's
# hand-built kanji-practice prototype, its build and mining scripts, generated PDFs and a zip,
# plus Krivi/old/ (~240 files including 214 stroke PNGs). None of it is served, none of it is
# referenced by any page, and committing generated binaries to a GitHub-Pages repo is the wrong
# home for them. Ignored rather than deleted: the files stay on disk untouched.
/Krivi/

# Commit-message scratch files. The house workflow writes `.commit_msg.tmp` and passes it to
# `git commit -F`, so these recur on every commit and should never be tracked.
.commit_msg.tmp

# Patch-script backups (added 2026-09-30). Every data/KB patch script copies its target to
# `<name>.bak_<purpose>` or `<name>.bak_<purpose>_<timestamp>` before writing, which is the right
# safety habit but leaves 34 files sitting in `git status` and hiding real untracked work - that is
# how three stroke-order SVGs went uncommitted for months. Git is the history for tracked files, so
# these never belong in it. Ignored, not deleted: the backups stay on disk.
*.bak_*
*.bak.json
